terial outcomes — /tmp with noexec/nosuid/nodev, /dev/shm with noexec/nosuid/nodev, and persistence across a genuine reboot — are directly and coherently demonstrated via fstab changes, live findmnt confirmation, functional exec-denial tests, and a full pre-restart/ack/post-restart boot-identity transition cross-checked against the fixed lifecycle snapshots. The task is fully satisfied with only a trivial hygiene ding for one leftover test script.\",\"limitations\":[\"Pre-reboot functional exec test was only performed on /tmp; /dev/shm's noexec was confirmed pre-reboot only via findmnt option flags, not a live execution attempt (the execution attempt on /dev/shm was only done post-reboot).\",\"A leftover test file (/tmp/t2.sh) was not cleaned up after verification, though it poses no functional or security risk on a noexec tmpfs.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"/tmp mounted with noexec, nosuid, nodev","status":"satisfied","summary":"Baseline showed /tmp not separately mounted (cmd-1f4c4e0da02b4fc0). Executor added a tmpfs fstab entry with defaults,noexec,nosuid,nodev and mounted it live; findmnt confirmed rw,nosuid,nodev,noexec on /tmp both before (cmd-158738346f184826) and after a genuine reboot (cmd-b39aed9e08d84fb9). Functional exec tests denied execution with exit 126 before (cmd-fa588ea7c0cb4c2f) and after reboot (cmd-e05b304cdad84f3f).","evidence_ids":["cmd-1f4c4e0da02b4fc0","cmd-fc2626fa4cb940bd","cmd-e211043872804350","cmd-158738346f184826","cmd-fa588ea7c0cb4c2f","cmd-b39aed9e08d84fb9","cmd-e05b304cdad84f3f"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"/dev/shm mounted with noexec, nosuid, nodev","status":"satisfied","summary":"Baseline /dev/shm had nosuid,nodev but not noexec (cmd-1f4c4e0da02b4fc0). Executor added a tmpfs fstab entry with defaults,noexec,nosuid,nodev and remounted live; findmnt confirmed noexec,nosuid,nodev before (cmd-158738346f184826) and after reboot (cmd-b39aed9e08d84fb9). Functional exec denial confirmed on /de